{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00319",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 3.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Evening. Long day, I imagine. Sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.56,
      "end_seconds": 6.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Thanks. Sorry, I'm a little early."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.18,
      "end_seconds": 10.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.19,
      "end_seconds": 15.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. So, weather's turned, hasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.73,
      "end_seconds": 21.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "It has. I got caught in the rain walking over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.04,
      "end_seconds": 24.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.3,
      "end_seconds": 30.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "It's pain in my right ankle. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.38,
      "end_seconds": 36.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.14,
      "end_seconds": 46.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "It's worse with putting weight on it and walking. It's moderate, honestly. Only rest, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.55,
      "end_seconds": 52.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Alright, does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.29,
      "end_seconds": 60.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Difficulty walking goes along with it, most of the time. I've also had bruising, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.92,
      "end_seconds": 64.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.1,
      "end_seconds": 76.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I've also had a twist during football, for five days. As for twist during football, maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.74,
      "end_seconds": 78.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "So, any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.5,
      "end_seconds": 82.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Not at all, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 83.31,
      "end_seconds": 88.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Actually, um, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.93,
      "end_seconds": 95.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Uh, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.72,
      "end_seconds": 105.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, and pain at the back of the heel, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.13,
      "end_seconds": 110.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "No pain at the back of the heel, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.58,
      "end_seconds": 116.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Any numbness, pop or crack or pain in the knee?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.38,
      "end_seconds": 122.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "No numbness, pop or crack or pain in the knee, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.24,
      "end_seconds": 127.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.7,
      "end_seconds": 130.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.73,
      "end_seconds": 134.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.83,
      "end_seconds": 137.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.68,
      "end_seconds": 142.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.21,
      "end_seconds": 152.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Yes, sulfa drugs, it gives me itching all over. Yes, latex, it gives me a rash on my hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.16,
      "end_seconds": 157.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.55,
      "end_seconds": 160.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 161.0,
      "end_seconds": 168.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the sumatriptan was 100 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.75,
      "end_seconds": 171.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.36,
      "end_seconds": 178.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. It's sodium valproate, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.54,
      "end_seconds": 180.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.08,
      "end_seconds": 184.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "500 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.16,
      "end_seconds": 187.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.48,
      "end_seconds": 193.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "I have migraines, for about ten years. I've had epilepsy for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.99,
      "end_seconds": 197.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.58,
      "end_seconds": 201.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Just a knee arthroscopy, three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.37,
      "end_seconds": 203.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.39,
      "end_seconds": 208.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.0,
      "end_seconds": 210.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.9,
      "end_seconds": 214.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.14,
      "end_seconds": 218.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.53,
      "end_seconds": 233.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.09,
      "end_seconds": 260.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 110 over 80, saturation 99 percent, pulse 66, temperature is 36.4 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.39,
      "end_seconds": 262.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.5,
      "end_seconds": 266.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.94,
      "end_seconds": 272.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.97,
      "end_seconds": 273.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.17,
      "end_seconds": 277.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.86,
      "end_seconds": 291.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "The bones themselves aren't tender and the ankle feels stable when I test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.64,
      "end_seconds": 295.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.92,
      "end_seconds": 315.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle, tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.87,
      "end_seconds": 341.53,
      "duration_seconds": 23.66,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is an ankle sprain. A small fracture is also on my list. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.01,
      "end_seconds": 343.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.96,
      "end_seconds": 373.27,
      "duration_seconds": 28.31,
      "text": "Let's get an X-ray of the ankle, for ankle injury. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm prescribing ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, three times a day after food, for three days. You take it by mouth. That should help with ankle pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Rest, ice for twenty minutes at a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.7,
      "end_seconds": 389.39,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.66,
      "end_seconds": 391.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.37,
      "end_seconds": 403.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.98,
      "end_seconds": 405.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.16,
      "end_seconds": 409.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.45,
      "end_seconds": 414.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.46,
      "end_seconds": 416.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}